;; Uncovered classes, and the authority a service in that class would have to
;; cite. NOT a generated file: appended one or two entries at a time by the
;; itonami-coverage-scout bot, and every entry re-checked at entry time by
;; scripts/itonami-verify-proposal.cljs.
;;
;; WHAT THIS FILE IS FOR, AND WHY IT IS NOT DERIVED
;;
;; The gap list itself IS derivable -- scripts/itonami-growth-evidence.cljs
;; computes it every run from the UN mirrors and manifest/west.yml, and nothing
;; here is allowed to disagree with that computation (the gate recomputes it and
;; ignores whatever an entry claims). What is not derivable is the third column:
;; which real authority a service in that function has to answer to. That is the
;; thing an actor built for this class will need on its first day, it cannot be
;; read off a classification table, and it is the only reason this file exists.
;;
;; So: the gap is measured, the authority is proposed and then fetched.
;;
;; ENTRIES ARE DELETED WHEN THE GAP CLOSES.
;;
;; Per ADR-2607257000 a document states the present, not its own history. When a
;; project is registered for a class, its entry is removed -- the gate will
;; reject re-adding it anyway, because it recomputes coverage from west.yml.
;; `git log -p` holds what was here before.
;;
;; SHAPE — tx-data, like every other EDN corpus here:
;;   (d/transact conn (edn/read-string (slurp "90-docs/coverage/itonami-coverage.datoms.edn")))
;;
;;   :coverage/kind          :cofog-group | :isic-class   (the gate judges only these two)
;;   :coverage/code          "091" (3 digits, COFOG) | "2520" (4 digits, ISIC)
;;   :coverage/name          the class name as the official table gives it
;;   :coverage/authority-url the authority a service in this class must answer to.
;;                           FETCHED by the gate at entry time. Not the
;;                           classification page -- that proves the class exists,
;;                           which was already measured.
;;   :coverage/jurisdiction  which jurisdiction that authority is for
;;   :coverage/verified-at   the day the gate fetched it
;;   :source/dataset         "itonami-coverage" -- joins on manifest/edn-query.cljs
;;
;; :coverage/code joins to repo-taxonomy's :repo/path once a project exists, and
;; to the scorecard's section fold via the first two digits.
